From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: map GetThemeSysColor's colour index to the theme's colour

Purpose: return the theme's caption text colour and the other system
colours that a theme defines.
Wine before: GetThemeSysColor looked up the COLOR_* index itself as a
property id, so COLOR_CAPTIONTEXT (9) never found TMT_CAPTIONTEXT (1610)
and the call fell back to the classic colour.
Change: look up TMT_FIRSTCOLOR + index for indices within the colour range.
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/uxtheme/nf-uxtheme-getthemesyscolor
Scope: documented API behaviour, for every Wine application.
Old patches: 0014 (its metric.c part).
---
 dlls/uxtheme/metric.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/metric.c b/dlls/uxtheme/metric.c
index 3ef199b..5fd573d 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/metric.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/metric.c
@@ -76,7 +76,8 @@ COLORREF WINAPI GetThemeSysColor(HTHEME hTheme, int iColorID)
     TRACE("(%p, %d)\n", hTheme, iColorID);
     SetLastError(0);
     if(hTheme) {
-        if((tp = MSSTYLES_FindMetric(TMT_COLOR, iColorID))) {
+        if(iColorID >= 0 && iColorID <= TMT_LASTCOLOR - TMT_FIRSTCOLOR
+           && (tp = MSSTYLES_FindMetric(TMT_COLOR, TMT_FIRSTCOLOR + iColorID))) {
             COLORREF color;
             hr = MSSTYLES_GetPropertyColor(tp, &color);
             if(SUCCEEDED(hr))
